DMS takes the first backlight it lists as the screen's, and listed them by
name.  A MacBook Pro with a Touch Bar has two: the bar's (raw,
"228600000.dsi.0") came before the screen's (platform, "apple-panel-bl"),
and the brightness slider and keys changed the bar.  Here backlights are
listed in the kernel's order of preference by their type, as systemd and
GNOME choose: firmware, platform, raw; by name after that.  Fit to send
upstream.

